  <title>Verbosity</title>
  <p>
    Use verbosity settings and commands to control how much information Orca includes in spoken
    output.
  </p>
  <p>
    Toggle speech verbosity level switches between brief and verbose object presentation. Other
    settings control individual details independently.
  </p>
  <p>
    For related settings, see <link xref="features_text_attributes#settings-checking-formatting">Text Attributes preferences</link>.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-verbosity">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Speech</gui> category, <gui>Verbosity</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>General</gui>: Controls overall speech
          detail.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>System messages are detailed</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca uses detailed messages or brief alternatives for Orca-specific information.
              Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Object presentation is detailed</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca provides brief or detailed object descriptions. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Spoken Object Details</gui>: Controls which
          object, text, and formatting details Orca speaks.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Only speak displayed text</gui>: When enabled, Orca
              speaks only text displayed on screen and omits extra details such as role, state,
              and misspelling indicators. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Description</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks the description supplied by the application in addition to an object's
              name. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Position in set</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks an item's position in a set, such as item 6 of 7. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Mnemonics</gui>: Controls whether Orca
              speaks object mnemonics, such as Alt+O for an OK button. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Tutorial messages</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks extra information about how to interact with the focused object.
              Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Blank lines</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks blank lines when navigating document content. When disabled, Orca says
              nothing when you move to a blank line. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Misspelled-word indicator</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca announces the misspelled-word indicator when you move into a misspelled word
              or type a word that the application marks as misspelled. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Text attribute changes</gui>: Controls when Orca
              speaks text formatting changes. Choices: Off (default), Editable text only,
              Always.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Indentation</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks indentation information for text content. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Only speak indentation if changed</gui>: Controls whether
              indentation is announced only when it changes from the previous line. Default:
              off.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="verbosity-commands">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Speech and verbosity</gui> group.
    </p>
    <section id="commands-verbosity-and-details">
      <title>Verbosity and details</title>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Toggle speech verbosity level</gui>
            <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>V</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
    <section id="commands-indentation">
      <title>Indentation</title>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Toggle spoken indentation</gui> Unbound by default.
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
</page>
